  "summary_en": "Adds density to a Float VDB using an envelope shape defined by Mono layers, combined with the existing VDB values through a chosen method (Add, Copy, Maximum, Average, Blend, Pull). The page states the node is available since 22.0.",
  "inputs": [
    "source: Float VDB to modify",
    "thickness: Mono layer setting the envelope thickness at each pixel",
    "height: Mono layer setting where the envelope centre line sits",
    "density: Mono layer setting the envelope density"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Method: how envelope values combine with current VDB values (Add, Copy, Maximum, Average, Blend, Pull)",
    "Border: overrides the border mode used when sampling the reference layers; Auto uses the input layer mode",
    "Shape: Acceleration and Deceleration (pull strength toward current values), Blend, Scale, Thickness (global scale for the thickness input), Scale by Timestep, Falloff",
    "Enable Noise: scales envelope values with noise; Noise Scale, Element Size, Element Scale, Noise Offset, Noise Pulse",
    "Enable Distortion: distorts the envelope shape with noise; Distort Scale, Element Size, Element Scale, Distort Offset, Distort Pulse"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "The node does not activate voxels, so sources outside already-active areas have no effect",
    "Requires DOP-level permissions; not in Houdini Core, only in Houdini FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education"
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Pyro Source from Layer ajoute de la densité à un VDB à partir d'une enveloppe dessinée par des calques Mono, sans activer de voxels nouveaux."
